[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 803,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 607,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122797,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 607,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Parathyroid lipoadenoma is a benign parathyroid neoplasm characterized by an unequivocal increase in parenchymal parathyroid tissue associated with abundant adipose tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 804,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 608,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122798,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 608,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8324/0 Parathyroid lipoadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 805,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 609,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122799,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 609,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F37.Y &amp; XH8P28 Other specified benign neoplasm of endocrine glands &amp; Lipoadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 806,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 610,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122800,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 610,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> parathyroid hamartoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 807,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 611,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122801,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 611,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 808,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 612,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122802,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 612,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Parathyroid lipoadenomas can arise in normally positioned glands, predominantly in left-sided locations {26585863}. Ectopic sites have also been reported, most commonly the mediastinum {7258157; 7364585; 26585863}. Subsets of patients develop multiglandular disease with two or more enlarged glands exhibiting abundant fat, termed lipohyperplasia {6648802; 18813123; 32193823}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 809,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 613,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122803,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 613,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most parathyroid lipoadenomas are functioning, and patients usually exhibit mild biochemical evidence of hyperparathyroidism with classic symptomatology {26585863; 32193823; 31773224}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 810,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 614,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122804,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 614,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fewer than 100&nbsp;cases have been reported in the literature {32193823}. A slight female predominance and a mean age of 56&nbsp;years are noted {26585863}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 811,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 615,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122805,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 615,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown. There is no known hereditary predisposition. An association with hypertension has been suggested {32193823}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 812,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 616,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122806,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 616,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The underlying molecular events are unknown.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 819,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 623,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122807,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 623,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The reported size and glandular weights vary, and parathyroid lipoadenomas tend to be larger than parathyroid adenomas {26585863}, with mean weights &gt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;g reported in some case series {18813123}. Tumours are often encapsulated and display a yellow cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 813,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 617,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122808,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 617,
        "headingText": "<p>The diagnosis should be restricted to adenomas with a significant increase in both adipose and parenchymal tissue {31773224}. Parathyroids that are enlarged solely because of an accumulation of adipose tissue but without an increase in parenchymal content should not be considered lipoadenoma {31773224}. Similarly, the presence of some adipose tissue in an otherwise typical parathyroid adenoma should not warrant the diagnosis {32193823}. A useful general rule is that &gt;&nbsp;50% of the volume of the gland should be adipose tissue to warrant the diagnosis {32193823}. The stromal component may include brown fat and myxoid or fibrous differentiation {26585863; 32193823}. A rim of compressed non-tumorous parathyroid tissue is usually present.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-11-29T15:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 814,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 618,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122809,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 618,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 815,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 619,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122810,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 619,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 818,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 622,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122811,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 622,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a definite increase in both parenchymal and adipose tissue in a parathyroid tumour; &gt;&nbsp;50% of the glandular volume is adipose tissue.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> a significant drop in intraoperative PTH or evidence of postoperative biochemical cure, or additional parathyroid gland(s) without a pathological diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 816,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 620,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122812,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 620,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 817,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 621,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 122813,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 69,
        "headingId": 621,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipoadenomas are benign. A series from Sweden suggested that patients with hyperparathyroidism treated by removal of lipoadenoma may have a lower initial biochemical cure rate and higher recurrence rate than those treated by removal of usual adenoma; however, this observation requires further validation {32193823}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:29:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]